{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And the children struggled within her — of the language of one running toward another runner: they were running and shifting about inside her body in the manner of fetuses. And so too: from קם comes מתקוממים, from לן comes מתלוננים. But from the language of רצץ, 'he crushed the needy,' it would have said וירצצו, as in ״בטרם יתנגפו רגליכם״." "To inquire of YHWH — to the prophets who were in those days, as it is written: ״לדרוש את ה' מאתו״. And it is written: ״כי יבא אלי העם לדרוש את ה'״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites Isaiah 3:15 (רצץ עזב דלים) and Proverbs 3:26 (בטרם יתנגפו רגליכם) to argue on morphological grounds that the hitpa'el form ויתרוצצו derives from רצץ 'run,' not רצץ 'crush.'", 1 "The first unaddressed quotation is from 2 Kings 22:18 (or 2 Chronicles 34:26); the second is from Ezekiel 14:1 (or 20:1)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:14.348208518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}